.TH UNHEADED\-KEYGEN 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 6b26b19a" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
unheaded\-keygen \- Create, rotate and retire service identity keys (Ed25519) and ML\-DSA\-65 signing keys.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unheaded\-keygen
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
SERVICE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create, rotate and retire service identity keys (Ed25519) and ML\-DSA\-65 signing keys.
SERVICE is the service's auth identity (the name it passes to auth.LoadServiceAuthConfig). An mldsa65 NAME is the key's file name (heimdall\-drift, akira\-health).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-algo \fISTRING\fR
ed25519 (service identity key) or mldsa65 (ML\-DSA\-65 signing key: drift, signed topics) (default ed25519)
.TP
.B \-\-dir \fISTRING\fR
directory for <service>.key and <service>.pub (default /etc/unheaded/keys)
.TP
.B \-\-owner \fISTRING\fR
chown the private key to this user name or uid[:gid] (root only)
.TP
.B \-\-print\-kid
print the current key id and exit
.TP
.B \-\-retire \fISTRING\fR
remove the rotated\-out public key with this kid from the trust directory
.TP
.B \-\-rotate
replace an existing key; keep its public half trusted until \-retire
.TP
.B \-\-trust\-dir \fISTRING\fR
trust directory every verifier reads (default /etc/unheaded/trust.d)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit codes: 0 done; 1 I/O or key file error; 2 usage error or refused (key exists, nothing to rotate, unknown or current kid, \-owner without root).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
unheaded\-keygen [\-dir D] [\-trust\-dir T] [\-owner U] SERVICE    create a key pair
unheaded\-keygen \-rotate [\-owner U] SERVICE                    new key, old public half kept
unheaded\-keygen \-retire KID SERVICE                           drop a rotated\-out public key
unheaded\-keygen \-print\-kid SERVICE                            print the current key id
unheaded\-keygen \-algo mldsa65 [\-dir D] [\-owner U] NAME        ML\-DSA\-65 signing key
unheaded\-keygen \-algo mldsa65 \-print\-kid NAME                 print its key id and public key
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
